.TH ESDM\-ES\-PCSC 8 "2026-11-06" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-es\-pcsc \- serve the random number generator of a smart card to the ESDM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-es\-pcsc
.RB [ \-\-reader
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-challenge_len
.IR N ]
.B \-\-socket
.I PATH
.RI [ "provider options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-es\-pcsc
asks a smart card for random bytes with GET CHALLENGE of ISO/IEC 7816\-4
through pcscd, which nearly every card answers without an application or a
PIN, and serves them as an external entropy source, which
.B esdm\-server \-\-es_ext
reads.
.PP
It uses the card of the first reader holding one. A card that is missing,
pulled or reset, or a pcscd restarted, is set up anew on the next request. A
card is tested when it is connected and on every self test of the ESDM \- two
reads of 16 bytes that must differ \- and one repeating itself is credited with
nothing until it passes again. No card is no reason not to serve: the ESDM
credits nothing meanwhile.
.SH NAME, RATE AND STATUS
The source declares the name
.B PC/SC
and no entropy rate: its data is claimed at 8 bits per byte, and what the card
is worth is for its assessment to say \- see
.B \-\-entropy_rate
of
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3)
and
.B \-\-es_ext_entropy_rate
of
.BR esdm\-server (8).
Its status names the
.BR reader ,
the
.B atr
of the card, the
.B repetition_test
.RB ( none ", " passed ", " failed ),
the counts of
.BR requests ,
.BR bytes ,
.B failures
and
.BR connects ,
and the
.BR last_error .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reader " \fINAME\fR"
Use only the reader whose name contains
.IR NAME .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-challenge_len " \fIN\fR"
The bytes asked for with one GET CHALLENGE, 1 to 255, by default 32.
.TP
.I provider options
.B \-\-socket
and the others of
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3).
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
esdm\-es\-pcsc \-\-socket /run/esdm\-es\-pcsc.socket \-\-entropy_rate 128
esdm\-server \-\-es_ext /run/esdm\-es\-pcsc.socket
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-server (8),
.BR esdm\-es\-pkcs11 (8),
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3),
.BR pcscd (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Markus Theil <theil.markus@gmail.com>
